  "id": "ana-everyone-s-happy-campaign",
  "name": "ANA Everyone's Happy Campaign",
  "category": "campaign",
  "description": {
    "text": "All Nippon Airways held its Everyone's Happy Campaign (みんなにうれしいキャンペーン) for the launch of its Pokémon Jet '99. Passengers who flew ANA within Japan between 1 June and 31 July 1999 and mailed two boarding pass stubs on the campaign postcard got Flying Pikachu and Articuno, as many times as they liked; flights in August and September brought Moltres and Zapdos instead. ANA called them the \"Pokémon Card ANA Special '99 Version\". Toshinao Aoki drew all four; the three legendary birds' pictures join into one when the cards are laid side by side, and his winking Flying Pikachu has an airliner on the left of the picture, where ANA's 1998 Flying Pikachu has it on the right.",
    "sources": [
      {
        "title": "ANA press release, 14 May 1999: \"Everyone's Happy Campaign\" (Japanese)",
        "url": "https://www.ana.co.jp/pr/990406-J/990514_2.html"
      },
